__pycache__
*.pyc
.venv
venv
.env
.git
.gitignore

# Model weights are DELIBERATELY not baked into the image — they are mounted
# read-only from the host by docker-compose.prod.yml (./models:/app/models:ro).
# Baking is not an option anyway: models/* is gitignored, so a build from a
# clean checkout would have nothing to copy. Only the manifest ships, so
# scripts/download_models.py has something to check against inside the
# container. Unlike git, Docker DOES honour an exception under an excluded
# parent directory, so the line below is load-bearing — see
# tests/test_deployment_config.py::TestDockerBuildContext.
models/
!models/manifest.json

# Training data and training outputs. Training-Images/ alone is ~16 GB; leaving
# these in meant every `docker build` shipped ~16 GB to the daemon before the
# first instruction ran, which is why a production build was never completed.
Training-Images/
runs/
benchmarks/

# Local C++ build artifacts — the extension is optional and every call site has
# a pure-Python fallback, so the image never needs a host-compiled .pyd.
build/
*.pyd
*.egg-info

# Training checkpoints left at the repo root (yolov8n-cls.pt). The image loads
# .onnx exports only — BibDetector refuses non-.onnx paths outright.
*.pt

tests/
*.md
.mypy_cache
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
htmlcov
